{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You were brought in today because of weakness and confusion. Can you tell me how you’ve been feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been really weak since this morning. I felt confused when I woke up. I’ve been trying to stay hydrated like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your calcium level came back high at 10.7, which can cause confusion and weakness. This is related to your multiple myeloma. We’ll start IV fluids right away to help bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time they gave me pamidronate. Why not this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had that treatment less than a week ago, so we can’t repeat it yet. Instead, we’ll use nasal calcitonin and fluids. It works quickly and safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My sugars have been high too—my wife said I was over 600 last week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood sugar was 358 when you arrived. The steroids you received in clinic can make that worse. We’ll monitor closely and adjust your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on glargine at night. Should I keep that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:25:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep your glargine and add a sliding scale. Our diabetes team will help fine-tune it. You may need more insulin while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. My kidneys were a little off last time too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-11-27 17:27:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is 1.3 today, which is slightly elevated. We’ll give fluids carefully and avoid any medications that could hurt your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-11-28 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night show your calcium is coming down. We’ll keep the IV fluids going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-11-28 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel a bit more alert today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-11-28 08:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely because your calcium is improving. We also checked a chest X-ray—no pneumonia, which is great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-11-28 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had a bit of a cough. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-11-28 08:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be from dryness or irritation. Your flu test was negative, and cultures didn’t show infection. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-11-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar spiked to over 450 yesterday. We put you on a short insulin drip to get it under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-11-29 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t realize it got that high. Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-11-29 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be if it stays high. But we caught it quickly. You’re back on subcutaneous insulin now, and we’ve increased your glargine to 35 units at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-11-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll check my sugars more often at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-11-29 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re giving you a new glucometer and strips. Please check four times a day—fasting and after meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine went up to 1.7, but it’s now back down to 1.2. That’s a good sign your kidneys are recovering."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of the fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Dehydration and high calcium can stress the kidneys. We’ve been careful with your fluid balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling short of breath when I walk to the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed that. It could be from a bit of fluid buildup, but your chest X-ray showed only mild changes. We’ve held back fluids to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could it be another blood clot? I had those before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a fair concern. We did a V/Q scan, and it showed a low chance of a pulmonary embolism. Your heart rhythm and EKG were normal too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might be related to your myeloma or anemia. But given your history, we want to rule out heart issues. We’ve ordered a stress test after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I should call to schedule that, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-11-30 10:12:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please call the cardiology office this week. It’s a pharmacologic test, so you won’t need to walk on a treadmill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-12-01 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You mentioned more shortness of breath yesterday. We did a portable chest X-ray."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-12-01 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any new fluid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-12-01 08:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No new pleural fluid or pneumothorax. Your Port-A-Cath is in good position. We think your symptoms may be chronic from your overall condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-12-01 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do get tired easily these days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-12-01 08:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with advanced myeloma. We’re continuing your bortezomib and dexamethasone to control the disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your calcium is now 9.5—well within normal range. Great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. And my sugars?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Much better—around 250. Still high, but stable. Keep checking at home and call your endocrinologist if it goes above 180 or below 80."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. What about the vancomycin I’m on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing it every six hours to prevent C. diff, especially since you’ve had it before and are on multiple medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve been constipated though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-12-02 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can adjust your stool softeners. Let the nurse know if it gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re planning to discharge you today. Your calcium is normal, and you’re feeling more like yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Check your blood sugar four times daily. Take your new insulin dose—35 units of glargine at bedtime. Call endocrinology if sugars are out of range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stress test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, call to schedule that. Also follow up with oncology. We may consider denosumab for your calcium if it keeps rising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I’ll stay on top of everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-12-03 07:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’ll send all instructions and prescriptions home with you. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-12-03 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-12-03 10:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-12-03 10:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your exam looks good—alert, breathing well, no swelling. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-12-03 10:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-12-03 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our team is here for you. Call us if anything changes. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-12-03 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final update: your discharge labs are back. Hemoglobin is 7.3, which is low but stable. We’re not transfusing unless you feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-12-03 12:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay. I’ll watch for fatigue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-12-03 12:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. And remember, if you feel dizzy or very short of breath, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-12-03 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2176-12-03 12:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in follow-up soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2176-12-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will be here soon to take you home. Do you have any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2176-12-03 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Check sugars, call endocrinology, schedule stress test, follow up with oncology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2176-12-03 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2176-12-03 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2176-12-03 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you’re cleared for discharge. The vancomycin will now be four times a day at home, not every six hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2176-12-03 16:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Four times a day."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-11-27 16:58:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-12-03 18:36:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with weakness and confusion due to malignant hypercalcemia in the setting of relapsed refractory multiple myeloma. He had recently received pamidronate, so he was treated with IV fluids and nasal calcitonin instead. His hospital course was complicated by steroid-induced hyperglycemia requiring an insulin drip and subsequent insulin regimen adjustment, with glargine increased to 35 units nightly. His renal function fluctuated but stabilized with careful fluid management. He reported dyspnea on exertion, but imaging and V/Q scan ruled out pulmonary embolism or significant fluid overload; a pharmacologic stress test was arranged outpatient to evaluate for cardiac causes. He remained on oral vancomycin for C. diff prophylaxis and continued chemotherapy with bortezomib and dexamethasone. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to monitor blood glucose four times daily, follow up with endocrinology and oncology, and schedule a cardiac stress test.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypercalcemia",
      "Multiple myeloma in relapse",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Enterocolitis due to Clostridium difficile",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with hyperglycemia",
      "Hypertension",
      "Dyspnea",
      "Thrombocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Peripheral neuropathy",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism"
    ]
  }
}
